I tend to think of the domestic animals as the ideal pets for the early
levels. They grow up to be quite strong, they are easily retamable should
you get separated, they can be trained to steal from shops. Keep them well
and you have a pet that is very useful until somewhere around the Quest.
Only then will you want a stronger pet that can take on shopkeeps and
priests.

It's not only the strength, there's also other considerations, like
non-eating monsters that might get really nasty when they turn untame, that
make an early polymorph for your pet seem like too much of a gamble.

